support two way to using the `phone`:

Typescript
```typescript
import { phone } from 'phone';

import phone from 'phone';
```

JS
```javascript
const { phone } = require('phone');

const phone = require('phone').default;
```

This works similar to nl_before_class, but the option to modify newlines
before structs is somehow missing, as far as I can see.

Currently, we can do the following:

```cpp
int foo = 1;
class Bar {};
int baz = 2;
```

and

```
nl_before_class = 2
```

and we obtain

```cpp
int foo = 1;

class Bar {};
int baz = 2;
```

Alas, when we have

```cpp
int foo = 1;
struct Bar {};
int baz = 2;
```

this is currently not possible.

